Subject: [PATCH v2 0/9] hv: vmbus: make rings and host-visible buffers
 survive fragmentation without breaking CoCo

This is v2 of the VMBus ring-allocation series. v1 was posted
unversioned on 2026-09-17/18 as a two-patch series and proposed a plain
vzalloc() fallback for vmbus_alloc_ring(). Michael Kelley reviewed that
approach on 2026-09-22 and pointed out the problem it creates:
set_memory_decrypted() only works on physically contiguous direct-mapped
memory, so a vmalloc ring in an arm64 CCA or TDX guest without a
paravisor cannot be re-encrypted. The fallback would fix ordinary guests
and break confidential ones.

He asked for the opposite structure: build on Kameron Carr's
vmbus_alloc_buffer() (already upstream) rather than adding a second
allocator path next to it. This series is that rewrite.

